<p>Kind of. Maybe? I don't want to give too much of what I think it is away, but uh &#8212;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">author&nbsp;headcanon</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The idea behind Hyakumonogatari Kaidankai is that you tell all these scary stories, and with each tale, you create the right context for an even scarier story to appear &#8212; one that's <em>real</em>. Each story is, in a sense, one part of a multi-part evocation to summon a terrifying spirit. Basically: Hear enough scary stories and one might actually emerge.</p>
<p>3117 is something similar: A trap for people who consume scary stories. And both the Foundation and the GOC are full of scary stories &#8212; which means this story, whatever it is, would be scary as heck.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>ETA:</strong> To clarify:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">author&nbsp;headcanon+</a></div>
